# ShellCheck configuration — read automatically from the checked file's directory
# upward, so it applies to CI, local runs and editor plugins alike. One owner.

# `-x` alone does NOT follow `source "$SCRIPT_DIR/lib/log.sh"`. ShellCheck reduces
# that to `./lib/log.sh` and looks for it in the SOURCE PATH, which defaults to the
# current directory — the repo root in CI. Every one of our scripts sources
# lib/log.sh that way, so the CI job reported "Not following:" twenty-two times,
# exited non-zero, and had been red for as long as it had existed while its own
# comment claimed `-x` followed the files "so directives are honored across the
# boundary". It honored nothing. SCRIPTDIR resolves relative to the script being
# checked, which is what that comment always meant.
source-path=SCRIPTDIR
